# Type-check first, then build.
#
# The order matters: `next build` no longer type-checks (see next.config.js),
# so `typecheck` is what catches type errors — and it fails in ~9s warm instead
# of dying 9 minutes into a build. Only once types are clean do we pay for the
# build.
#
# This hook used to run `npm run build` alone, which meant every commit paid
# for a full cold TypeScript check inside the build: about 11 minutes.
npm run typecheck && npm run build
